# Firebase web configuration for Google sign-in + saved metadata profiles.
# Copy to .env.local and fill in YOUR project's public web identifiers
# (Firebase console → Project settings → Your apps → Web app). The API key
# below is a public project identifier, NOT a secret — data safety comes
# from firestore.rules (owner-only), never from hiding these values.
# IMPORTANT: values starting NEXT_PUBLIC_ are inlined at `next build` time.
# After editing, rebuild (`npm run build`) and redeploy the static `out/`.
# Without these values the app runs fully as a guest; only the Google
# profile/rewrite surfaces report "not configured".
#
# Free Spark plan notes: ~50k reads / ~20k writes per day, 1 GiB stored,
# ~10 GiB/month egress. This app reads the profile once per sign-in and
# writes only when you press Save — far below those quotas.
# Also add your Hostinger domain (and localhost for testing) under
# Firebase console → Authentication → Sign-in method → Authorized domains.

NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_API_KEY=
NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN=your-project.firebaseapp.com
NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=your-project-id
NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_APP_ID=1:123456789012:web:abcdef1234567890abcdef
